      "heightMm": 42.23,
      "rgb": true,
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://www.kingston.com/datasheets/KF560C40BBAK4-64.pdf",
          "publisher": "kingston",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-03",
          "docType": "datasheet",
          "fields": [
            "partNumber",
            "type",
            "moduleCapacityGb",
            "moduleCount",
            "speedMtps",
            "timings",
            "voltageV",
            "profiles",
            "heightMm"
          ],
          "title": "Memory Module Specifications KF560C40BBAK4-64 (Document No. 4810826A)",
          "locator": "p. 1 title \"64GB (16GB 2G x 64-Bit x 4 pcs.)\", \"DDR5-6000 CL40 288-Pin DIMM Kit\"; Description \"Each module kit supports Intel® Extreme Memory Profiles (Intel® XMP) 3.0\"; Factory Timing Parameters \"XMP Profile #1: DDR5-6000 CL40-40-40 @1.35V\"; Default Features \"Height 1.66” (42.23mm), w/heatsink\""
        },
        {
          "url": "https://www.kingston.com/en/memory/gaming/kingston-fury-beast-ddr5-rgb-memory",
          "publisher": "kingston",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-03",
          "docType": "product-page",
          "archiveUrl": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260729175546/https://www.kingston.com/en/memory/gaming/kingston-fury-beast-ddr5-rgb-memory",
          "fields": [
            "brand",
            "name",
            "series",
            "formFactor",
            "moduleCount",
            "heightMm",
            "rgb"
          ],
          "title": "Kingston FURY™ Beast DDR5 RGB Memory",
          "locator": "Specifications \"Kits of 4: 64GB, 128GB\" and \"Dimensions\" \"133.35 mm x 42.23 mm x 7.11 mm\"; Features \"Enhanced RGB lighting with new heat spreader design\"; comparison table, column \"Beast DDR5 RGB\": row \"Module Type\" \"UDIMM\", row \"Height\" \"42.23mm\"; filters listing KF560C40BBAK4-64 under \"6000MT/s\", \"64GB\", \"Kit of 4\", \"40\", \"Intel XMP\", \"Black\""
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "field": "timings",
          "text": "Kingston gives the XMP timings as CL40-40-40 (\"XMP Profile #1: DDR5-6000 CL40-40-40 @1.35V\") and no tRAS for the profile; the datasheet's \"Row Active Time (tRASmin)\" row, \"32ns(min.)\", sits under \"DEFAULT SPECIFICATIONS\" (the JEDEC default), not the XMP profile."
        },
        {
          "field": "profiles",
          "text": "The datasheet says \"Each module kit supports Intel® Extreme Memory Profiles (Intel® XMP) 3.0\" and lists three XMP profiles and no AMD EXPO profile; the product page files this part under the \"Profile Type\" filter value \"Intel XMP\", not \"AMD EXPO / Intel XMP\". The comparison table marks the Beast DDR5 RGB line as a whole \"AMD EXPO™ Certified\"; that applies to the kits under \"AMD EXPO / Intel XMP\", which do not include this part."
        },
        {
          "field": "formFactor",
          "text": "The product page's comparison table gives Beast DDR5 RGB \"UDIMM\" in its \"Module Type\" row (Renegade Pro is the RDIMM line); the datasheet calls the kit a \"288-Pin DIMM Kit\"."
        },
        {
          "field": "name",
          "text": "The colour is from the product page's colour filter (\"Black\") and its kit-of-4 product images (\"Kingston FURY™ Beast DDR5 RGB memory modules, in black, kit of 4\"); Kingston also sells the kit in white (KF560C40BWAK4-64)."
        },
        {
          "field": "rgb",
          "text": "The product page lists \"Enhanced RGB lighting with new heat spreader design\" under Features; the datasheet's text does not mention lighting."
        },
        {
          "text": "kingston.com answered our fetcher with a Cloudflare challenge on 2026-10-03 (HTTP 403, \"Just a moment...\"), so the product page was read from its Wayback copy of 2026-07-29, the newest one the Wayback index holds with HTTP 200 (its 2026-09-05 capture is a 403); the datasheet PDF loaded directly."
        }
      ]
    }
